    "type": "message",
    "user": "U0CED0272DP",
    "text": "Hello,\n\nI wanted to ask about OLake's mapping of MySQL `DECIMAL` columns to `DOUBLE` in Iceberg rather than preserving their precision and scale.\n\nFor example, our MySQL `DECIMAL(18,2)` columns become Iceberg `DOUBLE` columns. This introduces a potential loss of precision for financial data, even though both MySQL and Iceberg support exact decimal types natively.\n\nIs this a deliberate architectural decision, or a current connector limitation? Are there plans to support native Iceberg `DECIMAL` types?",
    "ts": "1793698454.585819",
